  "question": {
    "text": "One mole of an ideal gas expands isothermally and reversibly from $10 \\mathrm{dm}^3$ to $20 \\mathrm{dm}^3$ at $300 \\mathrm{~K}. \\Delta \\mathrm{U}$, q and work done in the process respectively are :<br />Given : $\\mathrm{R}=8.3 \\mathrm{JK}^{-1}$ and $\\mathrm{mol}^{-1}$<br />$\\begin{aligned}<br />& \\text { In } 10=2.3 \\\\<br>& \\log 2=0.30 \\\\<br>& \\log 3=0.48<br />\\end{aligned}$"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$0,21.84 \\mathrm{~kJ},-1.26 \\mathrm{~kJ}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$0,-17.18 \\mathrm{~kJ}, 1.718 \\mathrm{~J}$",
